  "notes": "Sprint 137+ .dashboard parse error ghost pattern fixed with 3-layer approach:\n\n(A) Error Exposure: Replaced bare catch{} in status.ts with readDashboardSafe() that logs real error details via debugLog (stack trace, error type, file state). Error messages now include actual JSON parse error details instead of generic 'Cannot parse dashboard file'.\n\n(B) Dashboard Manager: New src/monitor/dashboard-manager.ts (~180 LoC) with:\n  - ensureDashboard(projectRoot): Creates/repairs corrupt .dashboard files\n  - readDashboardSafe(projectRoot): Never-throw read with auto-repair for unparseable JSON\n  - mergeDashboardDefaults(): Fills missing fields from partial but parseable JSON (tolerant read)\n  - isDashboardState(): Runtime type guard for full validation\n  - validateDashboardSchema(): Descriptive field-level error reporting\n  - DASHBOARD_INITIAL_STATE: Canonical empty state constant\n\n(C) Schema Validation: validateDashboardSchema provides descriptive per-field error messages (e.g. 'sprint.id (must be string), progress.done (must be number)').\n\nKey design decision: Parseable JSON objects are always accepted via merge-with-defaults (no disk repair). Only unparseable JSON triggers disk repair. This prevents false positives from partial dashboard data written by auditor during mid-scan cycles.\n\nTest updates: 28 new tests + 6 existing test files updated for new error message format and debugLog mock.\n\ntsc --noEmit: 0 errors (excluding pre-existing sprint-finalizer issue from other task).\nvitest: 746/746 pass across tests/monitor/ + tests/mcp/.",
